  DIRECTOR: The day goes quiet in the best way: Hush's old machine hums its tune, the towels come re-folded twice over, and nine Beats of pieces go together with a sound like a coat being buttoned. The print sits up, finds it has a name-field on its own paperwork, and asks, very carefully, whether it may stay with you. Hush stamps the application and says, mildly, that it has already sent a copy up the pump-lift to the Court's schedule — so the Relief's reason about an unlicensed body has quietly stopped being true, and Brack Nine-Badges is reading its clipboard with a bad expression.

A finished thing is registered, and a registered thing is a who, and a who has no price. Whoever signs the guarantor line becomes responsible for a person: that signature is the whole cost, and nobody can sign it for anyone else.

Bresk — you asked Hush to finish it. Is your mark on that line?

ILM OF THE OPEN HAND: What are the four offers on the wall, and who made them?
  DIRECTOR: The four sheets: the Hegemony's harvest line with a Codon price already printed; the Parlour's folding licence; a hearth scrap offering only a bench and a bowl; and a Cartography of Membranes "pattern deposit" wanting the print's shape itself. Hush says mildly, "They all arrived before you did." The print says nothing at all.

Bresk — the guarantor line is still blank. Your mark?
