  DIRECTOR: Forty-one bodies ahead of you stop moving as you arrive. The brine tastes of copper and warm brass. Clerk Second-to-Last leans over the desk, a brass badge dangling from one claw, a form with eleven boxes open before Bresk. "You'll only need three of these boxes to be untrue, and I am not allowed to say which. Waiting in the queue pays — a full Beat winds one clock back a step."

Does Bresk read the first box, or does the Cohort do something else?
