  (chronicle for The Filing Gate, 6.0 s) At the Filing Gate, Clerk Second-to-Last presented a form with three false boxes concerning the Foundry’s patent and Line status. Bresk took the form while Ilm discovered the clerk had double-tallied the badge fee and misaligned deductions; the clerk corrected the ledger and muttered about third errors that week. Brost inspected the notice board, finding only repeated maintenance suspensions and a card for the Relief crew arriving on Beat 3. In the ledger, Third-of-Nine-Vat was crossed out three times, with an unclaimed licence hidden behind it. Vash asked if waiting would wind clocks, but the clerk warned the clocks were empty. Bresk signed for the cheapest wage, leaving the Foundry boxes blank. The clerk stamped a badge, and the Cohort passed through the Warden arch onto the brine-walk toward the Picket Hearth.
