BRESK OF THE SIXTH CHOIR: I take the bowl from the hearth and eat. Does anyone speak?
    [award] {"codon":0,"substrate":0,"why":"The hearth: a shared meal at the Row's soup line."}
  DIRECTOR: The soup is hot, salty, burnt at the edges — enough, not good. As Bresk eats, the row's conversation creeps back, and four hundred stopped machines hang overhead, one still clutching a shape its hand will never finish. A broad tired organ steps from behind the pot, badge-read in one claw. "Cheap wage, three boxes blank. Honest or slow — I'll take honest." Eyes turn to wait. "Whose wage are you on?" Ilm of the Open Hand, what do you answer?
