"Unlicensed crew," the nine-badged one says, "removing licensed material from the premises of record — organ one hundred and eighteen." It writes the words as it speaks them. That is the wrong reason, and forty shells heard the warranty read that address aloud. It says *assignment*, and adds a column of figures to its card.

Behind you the bench has not called ticket nine. The drafted decision is still face-down on the bench.

Bresk of the Sixth Choir — do you stand there and answer the charge with the warranty in your hand, or does the water go tight?
