  DIRECTOR: The way is not clear. The nine-badged one has not moved out of the corridor; it is still writing, and the two brass-jointed constructs stand exactly where a diagram would put them, with the squat tank ticking its hourly rhythm beside them. Behind you the drafted decision lies face-down on the bench, and if you walk out past it, it issues as written.

Ticket nine has not been called. Forty shells are turned toward the corridor, and a clerk at the arch edge has a fresh sheet and a stylus already uncapped, taking notes on whatever happens next.

Vash of the Long Reach — the Row knows you can carry people out of a stopped district faster than anyone. Do you try to put the four of you past the Relief into the alley, or does the water go tight here in front of forty witnesses?
